{
  "0": "Across all four datasets, scale only real history input embeddings by 1+0.03*min(n_t,20)/20, where n_t counts observed real items through position t. This causal prefix-length feature may distinguish established context from short prefixes without relying on repeated items. Keep padding zero, candidate embeddings unchanged, and preserve embedding parameterization, GRU topology, readout, loss and optimizer. Apply identical feature construction in the predictor writer.",
  "1": "Across all four datasets, replace strict unit normalization in the tied item embedding with e/max(||e||_2,1e-12)^0.9 for both history and candidate lookups, keeping padding zero. Retaining a small amount of jointly learned item magnitude may improve representation flexibility without adding parameters or a separate scorer. Preserve dimensions, GRU topology, features, history, readout, scoring formula, loss and optimizer; synchronize predictor loading.",
  "2": "Across all four datasets, shorten only the causal pooling half-life from three interactions to 2.5, retaining the incumbent 0.8*h_t+0.2*m_t blend. Since half-life three improved over four while reducing the pooled contribution regressed, modestly faster decay may sharpen recent interests while preserving pooling strength. Exclude padding and future states, retain final-real-position inference, and synchronize checkpoint metadata and the predictor writer. Keep all other settings fixed.",
  "3": "Across all four datasets, jointly reduce Adam learning rate from 1e-3 to 7e-4 and increase existing embedding dropout from 0.10 to 0.15. Stronger input regularization may reduce overfitting, while smaller updates may stabilize optimization under the additional dropout noise. Preserve features, embedding parameterization, dimensions, GRU depth, history, readout, scoring and loss. Retain seed 42, 200 batches per epoch, the 200-epoch cap and one checkpoint per category."
}
